From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_GBB_POSITION_INVARIANT and EDEN_GBB_NAN_GUARD: positions Invariant, float colour outputs without NaN

Port of GBB's patch 0915 (issue 21, 10 Nov 2026), under his switch names so one env file works on
both builds. The same fix ships in PS5_Lichii v1.20 as patch 0229 (Mihawk); it comes from
notquiteog/Dragoon 395547c and NX2navi patches 0007 and 0027.

- EDEN_GBB_POSITION_INVARIANT=1: gl_Position is decorated Invariant in every stage that writes
  it. A colour pass drawn again with depth EQUAL after a depth pre-pass then computes the same
  depth; without the decoration AMD's compiler may not, and the pixel fails the test.
- EDEN_GBB_NAN_GUARD=1: a float colour output is stored as 0 when it is NaN and clamped to
  +-1e30 otherwise. One NaN texel spreads through bloom and blur averages into blocks.

Both are off without the switch (exact "1"); upstream turns them on for every driver but
NVIDIA's. GBB on 13.60, with EDEN_NX2_MASK_COMPONENTS=1 and EDEN_NX2_MASK_UNWRITTEN=1: flashes
with one frame ahead went from a few per walk to nearly none, at no cost in fps.

Both change the SPIR-V of nearly every shader. The names are added to the prepared store's
stamp list, so a flip starts that store empty and the shader set converts again.

diff --git a/src/shader_recompiler/backend/spirv/emit_spirv_context_get_set.cpp b/src/shader_recompiler/backend/spirv/emit_spirv_context_get_set.cpp
index e8af2a5..b28fcec 100644
--- a/src/shader_recompiler/backend/spirv/emit_spirv_context_get_set.cpp
+++ b/src/shader_recompiler/backend/spirv/emit_spirv_context_get_set.cpp
@@ -518,6 +518,13 @@ void EmitSetFragColor(EmitContext& ctx, u32 index, u32 component, Id value) {
     const AttributeType type{ctx.runtime_info.color_output_types[index]};
     if (type == AttributeType::Float) {
         const Id pointer{ctx.OpAccessChain(ctx.output_f32, ctx.frag_color.at(index), component_id)};
+        if (ctx.profile.guard_frag_color_nan) {
+            // EDEN_GBB_NAN_GUARD: NaN becomes 0, anything else stays within +-1e30.
+            const Id clamped{ctx.OpNMin(ctx.F32[1],
+                                        ctx.OpNMax(ctx.F32[1], value, ctx.Const(-1e30f)),
+                                        ctx.Const(1e30f))};
+            value = ctx.OpSelect(ctx.F32[1], ctx.OpIsNan(ctx.U1, value), ctx.Const(0.0f), clamped);
+        }
         ctx.OpStore(pointer, MarkHotFragColor(ctx, component, value));
     } else if (type == AttributeType::UnsignedInt) {
         const Id pointer{ctx.OpAccessChain(ctx.output_u32, ctx.frag_color.at(index), component_id)};
